Write these sections using these exact headings:

## A. Learning Objectives and Success Criteria
- Clear, measurable objectives; what students should know or be able to do
- Simple "I can..." success criteria students understand
- The same core objective applies to every differentiated version

## B. Teacher Explanation (teacher-facing)
- Accurate, age-appropriate explanation in manageable steps
- Essential vocabulary with simple definitions
- Relatable examples and analogies
- Common misconceptions and how to address them

## C. Student Handout (student-facing)
- Short introduction, key concepts, examples, brief review
- Headings, bullet points, numbered steps, clear instructions
- No unnecessary information or excessive text

