## F. Examples and Activities
- At least 3 age-appropriate examples
- Guided practice and independent practice
- One interactive or hands-on activity (use the available resources)
- One visual or multisensory activity
- Short adaptation notes for Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced and Dyslexia-friendly

## G. Practice Exercises (student-facing, clear instructions)
Include: multiple-choice, matching or sorting, fill-in-the-blank with a word bank, short-answer, and one application or problem-solving task.

## H. Discussion Questions
Include: simple comprehension, "explain your thinking", real-life application, and extension questions for advanced learners. Add optional sentence starters and oral-response alternatives.

